-**Residual, for the lead to weigh**: the allow-list limits *which* files are committed, not *what is in them*. Four are executable code: `server/juice.js`, `server/salary.js`, `public/viz/palette.js` and `public/features/shared.js`. All four run in visitors' browsers: `palette.js` and `shared.js` directly, and `juice.js` and `salary.js` through `/lib/` (`server/lib-modules.js:11`). Hardening: after `apply`, run `git diff -U0 "$GITHUB_SHA" -- <those four>` and refuse unless every changed line has a shape the writers produce (`^[+-]\s*[A-Z]{3}: [0-9.e-]+,?$`, the `FX_AS_OF` / `FX_SOURCE` one-liners, the `FX_FALLBACK` CNY entry, the tax constants). In the first live refresh commit (`9de373f`), every changed line in those four files has one of these shapes: the FX table rows, `FX_AS_OF`, `FX_SOURCE` and the CNY fallback. So the check would not get in the way of a real refresh.
